  "final_answer_full": "The area of each ship has been calculated using the provided GSD of 0.431 meters per pixel. Each ship's area is determined by multiplying the number of pixels by the GSD squared (0.431²). The resulting areas are labeled on the image, which has been saved as `/data1/yuhongjie2/OpenEarthAgent/data/train_part1/dior_12269_bboxes_text.jpg`.\n\n**Key Steps:**\n1. **Detection:** Ships were identified using SAM2 segmentation, yielding 24 regions.\n2. **Area Calculation:** Each ship's area is calculated as:\n   $$\n   \\text{Area (m²)} = \\text{width (pixels)} \\times \\text{height (pixels)} \\times (0.431)^2\n   $$\n   For example, a ship with dimensions 148x48 pixels has an area of:\n   $$\n   148 \\times 48 \\times (0.431)^2 \\approx 148 \\times 48 \\times 0.185761 \\approx 1338.2 \\, \\text{m²}\n   $$\n3. **Visualization:** Bounding boxes and area labels are added to the image for clarity.\n\nThe final image with labeled ship areas is available at the specified path. Let me know if further analysis is needed!",
